{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558596-technocrats-and-the-discarding-of-instruments","id":1558596,"title":"Technocrats and The Discarding of Instruments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-02T13:57:45-08:00","id":1558596,"title":"Technocrats and The Discarding of Instruments","content":"I have a couple of questions after reading the sections about Arete/Enlightment and how its progression relates to the discarding of instruments, especifically in relation to Technocrats:<br /> <br /> 1) Does the indoctrination of Technocrats demanding the use of Instruments even in high levels of Arete result in a disadvantage when dealing with mystics or technomancers in combat, or it's not that big of a deal in this context?<br /> <br /> 2) The paragraph in the section <i>Growing Beyond the Tools </i>of M20's Corebook, p. 567 kinda has a chilling prophecy for the Path of a Technocrat:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technocrats receive so much indoctrination that they never<br /> break through their preconceptions that way. Unless he leaves<br /> the Technocracy to pursue a different Path, a Technocrat remains<br /> convinced that his faction\u2019s perception of reality is the only one<br /> that truly works\u2026 and that perspective demands instruments<br /> of science, even if those instruments aren\u2019t always obvious. <b>At<br /> Arete 10, a Technocrat becomes part of the Machine \u2013 a focus<br /> for the Will of technology instead of the other way around.</b> </div> </div> </div>Does the Technocrat with Arete 10 just... lose their free will here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T16:13:17-08:00","id":1558598,"title":"","content":"1) I\u2019d say on a situation by situation analysis, it is a factor, but in general not really. A lot of the really big stuff requires planning and preparation so usually doesn\u2019t involve getting caught without tools.<br /> <br /> 2) It waxes a bit poetic so I\u2019d say it is optional. It is up to the table whether that\u2019s a real fate or just a rhetorical flourish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T19:22:58-08:00","id":1558606,"title":"","content":"It's the Cost of being on top Your version of magic is tied to your Focus, if the OoH was on top they would be Constructing Arrays and Chanting Spells till Ascension, DreamSpeakers would be Meditating, Chanting, Waving Fetishes and dropping Mystic Herbs and so on all to prevent the penaitiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T03:11:22-08:00","id":1558614,"title":"","content":"Psionics would be the most logical paradigm for a technocrat to perform magic without instruments. However I don't think the Technocratic Union tolerates Psionics anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T05:14:27-08:00","id":1558617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558596-technocrats-and-the-discarding-of-instruments#post1558596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Does the indoctrination of Technocrats demanding the use of Instruments even in high levels of Arete result in a disadvantage when dealing with mystics or technomancers in combat, or it's not that big of a deal in this context?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it. Whilst Technocrats are tied to their instruments, they're also the group most able to handwave stuff on the basis that the Technocracy has infrastructure everywhere already in place, or that their magic is simply the result of the mage's superlative qualities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Technocrat with Arete 10 just... lose their free will here? </div> </div> </div>Free will is a bit of a slippery concept, but I think the idea is more that by arete 10, you've reshaped yourself to the point that your free will is in line with the systems the Technocracy is based around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T05:38:02-08:00","id":1558618,"title":"","content":"I mean, Arete 10 it's the end of the road anyway. It's not something a PC will ever get on a normal game. I think that part talks more of what Apex Technocrats look like than any mechanical limitation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T16:57:11-08:00","id":1558624,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Technocracy is at a bit of a disadvantage in this regard due to the inability to work without Instruments. At lower levels of Arete, this drawback is shared with other Technomancers: as of Arete 5, mystics will have already specified two Instruments that are now optional, while technomancers of all stripes won't have specified any. And both Technomancers and Technocrats are completely unable to use the Work Without Focus rules of M20.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, the Technocracy arguably has an advantage that comes with this drawback: it can be argued that their focus on the importance of tools is what allows them to make facilities that let them produce Devices without needing to expend personal Quintessence or a dot of Willpower in doing so. In short, this drawback is coupled with the Union's ability to mass produce Devices.<br /> <br /> And when coupled with the option in M20 Sorcerer saying that mages can create Paths using essentially the same rules that exist for creating Talismans, the Technocracy arguably ought to have an edge in terms of techno-sorcery as well, letting them innovate new Procedures and then turn those Procedures into Techno-Sorcerous Paths that their Extraordinary Citizens can learn and wield. A mage creating a Path of Sorcery would need to expend a lot of personal Quintessence on the Arete rolls to set it up, and would need to finalize the whole thing by investing a dot of Willpower into it; the Technocratic counterpart could do the equivalent without either of those requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typo 03-04-2026, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T18:58:13-08:00","id":1558629,"title":"","content":"As for Arete 10: recall that the Technocracy has Control. Recall also that the Technocracy isn't really big on the pursuit of Ascension; at least, not <i>personal </i>Ascension. Even among the Traditions, Arete 10 doesn't equal Ascension; instead, high-Arete mages who <i>don't </i>seek Ascension end up with other fates such as becoming archmasters, Exemplars, or gods. I could see an Arete 10 Technocrat becoming part of Control, as the Technocratic equivalent of the non-Ascension fates of non-Technocracy mages. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Technocrats are <i>blocked </i>from achieving personal Ascension; as I said, Ascension isn't synonymous with Arete 10. The Technocracy doesn't provide any <i>guidance </i>to the Scientist who seeks personal Ascension (though that's also true of most of the Crafts, with the Batini and perhaps the Children of Knowledge and the Hollow Ones as exceptions proving the rule), and may even actively obstruct such efforts (personal Ascension is arguably unmutual); but personal Ascension is, in the end, <i>personal; </i>and whether or not it can be achieved ultimately depends on the individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T18:38:43-08:00","id":1558646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558596-technocrats-and-the-discarding-of-instruments?p=1558606#post1558606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Cost of being on top Your version of magic is tied to your Focus, if the OoH was on top they would be Constructing Arrays and Chanting Spells till Ascension, DreamSpeakers would be Meditating, Chanting, Waving Fetishes and dropping Mystic Herbs and so on all to prevent the penaitiles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems to be more of a conditioning than the result of being the dominant paradigm. Already in the order of reason time they had troubles discarding foci","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T06:43:44-08:00","id":1558661,"title":"","content":"And I do want to stress that it matters whether we are talking about quick spells popped off in the field and big efforts. For the small stuff, being able to work without instruments matters, as does getting the difficulty reduction for working with them after they are dropped. It gives the Traditions and others a versatility that the Technocrats will have a hard time matching. It also means that in the rare situation where they are caught without tools they are at an extreme disadvantage, though between emergency analysis* and seeded technology** they often still have options.<br /> <br /> Big efforts, on either side, are usually done with rituals, careful planning, and plenty of preparation. These will typically use the mage's instruments whether or not he's dropped them. And yes, using dropped instruments does make the spell easier, but so does careful study, planning, and preparation. It does mean that you could stop a Technocrat from using a ritual (or whatever they call it) by stealing or sabotaging one of the important machines for it, but honestly they should be able to disrupt a Traditions ritual (say, one Voormas is working on) by messing with the important components too. So for the big stuff the Technocracy is barely hindered at all. <br /> <br /> *Emergency Analysis - A Technocrat method of casting without tools. In the right circumstances Technocrat field agents can analyze their surroundings and &quot;calculate&quot; that a convenient event is about to happen (the ice is about to crack, the ladder is about to give way, etc. Think dramatic environmental effects in movies). The agent may or may not realize they are making the event happen, but it works either way.<br /> <br /> **Seeded technology - Some of the Conventions seed conventional technology (pun not intended) with small pieces of hypertech so that agents can sometimes use the technology around them for extraordinary effects. So often field agents are closer to their tools than it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T10:13:29-08:00","id":1558684,"title":"","content":"A follow-up question:<br /> <br /> What intrigues me about the idea of a Personal Ascension for a Technocrat (a topic I already asked about in another post) is how unlikely it seems. I know that Ascension is not defined exactly in the books and the ST has leeway to conceptualize Ascension on a table/player basis and also that Mage is more about seeking Ascension that achieving it. Even then, per the M20 corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As The Book of Mirrors points out (pps. 60-61), Ascension<br /> is not hitting Arete 10 or maxing out all your Spheres. It\u2019s not<br /> about power but about the transcendence of the need for power.<br /> Mere power, in Mage, is a trap. The more a mage pursues it, the<br /> further she gets from ultimate Ascension. </div> </div> </div>The thing is, everything about the Technocratic Union screams a &quot;need for power&quot;. Of course, that power can be used with benevolent intentions, guiding and uplifting the Masses, and all the sourcebooks since <i>Guide to The Technocracy</i> points to a more nuanced scenario than just souless mirroshades. But still, even with all the progress alluded to be possible in <i>Technocracy Reloaded, </i>the same sourcebook points to the totalitarian nature of the Union itself (p.113):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although the Union has always been considerably more<br /> complex than outside stereotypes would lead us to believe, the<br /> Technocracy remains \u2014 despite its current emphasis on reform<br /> \u2014 a fundamentally militaristic totalitarian engine of global<br /> control. </div> </div> </div>How can a Technocrat achieve Personal Ascension, if control (i.e. the need for power) is so integral to a Technocrat's identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T11:19:00-08:00","id":1558685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558596-technocrats-and-the-discarding-of-instruments?p=1558684#post1558684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a Technocrat achieve Personal Ascension, if control (i.e. the need for power) is so integral to a Technocrat's identity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have to go rogue and leave the Union. (Indeed, that may well be what you have to do, no matter what organisation you're a part of).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T11:38:55-08:00","id":1558686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558596-technocrats-and-the-discarding-of-instruments?p=1558684#post1558684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A follow-up question:<br /> <br /> How can a Technocrat achieve Personal Ascension, if control (i.e. the need for power) is so integral to a Technocrat's identity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you need to distinguish between the Technocracy's identity and a technocrat's identity, because they are not the same thing. It is at least reasonable that the former is an impediment to Personal Ascension, so a technocrat who embodies that identity would a) not even seek personal ascension and b) have problems achieving it if he did.<br /> <br /> But the first issue is, does the typical technocrat embody that identity? It's not at all necessary that the members of an organization themselves represent those ideals in all things. I'd say it isn't even that common, even among members who believe strongly in the organization. The principles that an organization works on do not always make for good principles for a person to live their life by. So we need to figure out what the typical technocrat identity gets in the way of personal ascension.<br /> <br /> And the second issue is... there's no such thing as a typical technocrat, in the same way there's no such thing as an average person. However we measure what is typical, normal, or average, that's just a generalization and it is rare to find an actual person who actually fits that measurement. So we need to figure out what parts of the &quot;typical technocrat&quot; identity get in the way of personal ascension and then look at how many actual technocrats have those elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T03:59:57-07:00","id":1558744,"title":"","content":"The way I'd phrase it is that a necessary condition of Personal Ascension for a member of the Technocracy would be to decide &quot;am I a technocrat, or am I an Enlightened Scientist?&quot; Technocrats are, by definition, people who believe in the rule of experts, and that they are the experts. Most members of the technocracy are, unsurprisingly, technocrats. Enlightened Scientists cover a wider scope: while they share theTechnocracy's Practices and Instruments, they don't necessarily share its Paradigms, such as Might Makes Right. Navalon is the closest thing to a canonical group of not-technocratic Enlightened Scientists in the game, though they have their own problems.<br /> <br /> As Michael pointed out, disengaging from the Ascension War and leaving whichever faction you;ve been in might be another necessary step for Personal Ascension.<br /> <br /> What may <i>not</i> be required, though, is abandoning your Practices or Instruments. If you think that a Technomancer's inability to Work Without Focus or a Technocrat's complete inability to surpass his Instruments completely blocks him from achieving personal Ascension, I'd just point out that that's the flip side of &quot;you must reach Arete 10 to Ascend&quot;: while raising Arete or surpassing Instruments can help achieve personal Ascension, neither is strictly necessary. The actual determination is narrative, not gamist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typo 03-09-2026, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}